---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Island from '../components/Island.astro';
import {product} from '../data/site';
import {release} from '../data/release';
---
<Layout title="Floatlet | Free Dynamic Island for Windows 11">
<section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-kicker"><span class="windows-icon" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span> DYNAMIC ISLAND, MADE FOR YOUR WINDOWS DESKTOP</div><h1>A little island.<br/><span>A calmer desktop.</span></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p>Your soundtrack. Your next meeting. Your moment to focus.<br/>A free, open-source Dynamic Island for Windows 11 that keeps the little things close.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href={release?.url||product.repository+'/releases'} data-event="download_click" data-placement="hero">Download for Windows <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="underlink" href="#experience">Try the island ↘</a><a class="underlink" href={product.repository} data-event="github_click">GitHub ↗</a><span class="fine">Free & open source · x64 preview · Unsigned</span></div></div></section>
<div class="product-strip wrap" aria-label="At a glance"><span>Native C++</span><span>No account required</span><span>Free &amp; open source</span><span>Windows 11 · x64</span></div>
<section class="experience wrap" id="experience" aria-label="Try Floatlet"><Island/></section>
<section class="feature-atlas wrap" aria-label="Floatlet at a glance">
<a href="#music" class="atlas-card"><span class="atlas-icon" aria-hidden="true">♫</span><small>YOUR SOUNDTRACK</small><h3>The cover.<br/>The chorus. The controls.</h3><p>Supported media sessions, artwork and a small waveform. Hover, skip, carry on.</p><span class="atlas-link">Explore music ↗</span></a>
<a href="#files" class="atlas-card"><span class="atlas-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span><small>YOUR IN-BETWEEN SPACE</small><h3>Drop it here.<br/>Pick it up there.</h3><p>A temporary shelf for file references. Your originals stay exactly where they belong.</p><span class="atlas-link">Explore the tray ↗</span></a>
<a href="#experience" class="atlas-card"><span class="atlas-icon" aria-hidden="true">◷</span><small>YOUR NEXT MOMENT</small><h3>Time to focus.<br/>Space to breathe.</h3><p>Clocks, persistent alerts and a shared agenda for up to eight calendar subscriptions.</p><span class="atlas-link">Try a moment ↗</span></a>
</section>
<section class="search-story wrap" id="search"><div><p class="eyebrow">IN DEVELOPMENT / FLOATLET SEARCH</p><h2>A thought.<br/>A shortcut.<br/><span>You're there.</span></h2><p>Find an app, an indexed file or a Floatlet command from Alt+Space. Matching apps come first. Keep a file in your tray without breaking your flow.</p><button class="button secondary" data-search-open>Try sample Search ↗</button><a class="underlink" href="/docs/search/">Explore Search and its requirements ↗</a></div><div class="search-art" aria-label="Illustration of Floatlet Search"><div class="search-art-query"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span> google<span class="keycap">esc</span></div><small>RESULTS</small><div class="search-art-row selected"><span class="app-tile">G</span><div><strong>Google Chrome</strong><small>Application</small></div><span>↵</span></div><div class="search-art-row"><span class="folder-tile">▰</span><div><strong>Google</strong><small>Sample folder</small></div></div><div class="search-art-footer"><span>↵ Open</span><span>⇧ ↵ Add to tray</span><span>⇥ Actions</span></div><p>Sample UI · not included in the 0.6.3 download</p></div></section>
<section class="intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">LESS SWITCHING. MORE DOING.</p><h2>The small things,<br/>a little closer.</h2><p>Skip a track. Keep a file handy. Turn the volume down. Floatlet brings everyday actions into one small surface, inspired by the Dynamic Island concept and built for Windows.</p></section>
<section class="story wrap" aria-label="Explore the island"><div class="story-rail"><span class="eyebrow">ONE LITTLE SPACE</span><h2>Room for<br/>your rhythm.</h2><a class="underlink" href="#experience">Back to the live preview ↑</a></div><div class="story-chapters"><article id="music"><span class="chapter-no">01 / MUSIC</span><h3>Keep the song.<br/>Lose the detour.</h3><p>Album artwork and playback controls from supported Windows media sessions. Hover for the next track, without hunting for your player.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="music">Try music controls ↗</button></article><article id="files"><span class="chapter-no">02 / TRAY</span><h3>A stop along<br/>the way.</h3><p>Drop a file reference into the tray, then drag it into another app when you're ready. Removing a reference leaves your original file untouched.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="files">Try the sample tray ↗</button></article><article id="controls"><span class="chapter-no">03 / CONTROLS</span><h3>Small adjustments.<br/>No big interruption.</h3><p>Volume, supported display brightness and nearby Wi-Fi. A timer when you need a moment. A calendar when you need to look ahead.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="controls">Try the controls ↗</button></article><article><span class="chapter-no">04 / CLOCK</span><h3>A moment to focus.<br/>A nudge when it ends.</h3><p>Timers and alarms expand into a persistent alert. A running stopwatch stays visible in the compact pill. Dismiss an alert when you are ready, not when a timeout decides.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="clock">Start a ten-second timer ↗</button></article><article><span class="chapter-no">05 / CALENDAR</span><h3>One day.<br/>All your calendars.</h3><p>Connect up to eight Google Calendar subscriptions. Browse a shared agenda, filter duplicate events, and get a pop-out within five minutes of a timed event. Private links stay encrypted on your PC.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="calendar">Explore the sample calendar ↗</button></article><article><span class="chapter-no">06 / YOUR SPACE</span><h3>Only what<br/>you want to see.</h3><p>Keep the music bar icon-only. Reduce motion. Hide microphone activity with Show calls. Floatlet stays in the background and can start with Windows.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="settings">Make the preview yours ↗</button></article></div></section>
<section class="honest wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">NATIVE BY DESIGN</p><h2>A small surface.<br/>An open project.</h2></div><div><p>Built with C++ and Windows composition. No bundled browser. No account required for the app.</p><p class="muted">This is an early preview. Some controls open Windows settings. Battery savings and 120 Hz smoothness have not been verified.</p><a class="underlink" href="/docs/capabilities/">What works, and what doesn't ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="evidence wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE REAL APP</p><h2>Source you can inspect.</h2><p>The playground uses original sample artwork and fictional events. It does not connect to Spotify, Discord or Google Calendar, play audio, or read files. The native app connects through supported Windows interfaces. See exactly what ships in the source, release notes and test evidence.</p><a class="underlink" href={product.repository} data-event="github_click">Explore the repository ↗</a></section>
<section class="home-faq wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2>Small island.<br/>Clear answers.</h2><a class="underlink" href="/dynamic-island-for-windows/">The Windows guide ↗</a></div><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is Floatlet?</summary><p>A free, open-source Dynamic Island app for Windows 11. It brings supported music playback, file references, system controls, clocks and optional calendar subscriptions into a compact desktop capsule.</p></details><details><summary>Is it just for Surface laptops?</summary><p>No. The x64 preview targets Windows 11 Intel and AMD PCs. Windows 11 ARM PCs can use x64 emulation. There is no native ARM64 download yet.</p></details><details><summary>Does it work with Spotify and Apple Music?</summary><p>The public app reads artwork and playback controls exposed by Windows media sessions. Browser behaviour varies. The development build adds an Apple catalogue artwork fallback; that change is not in the current public download.</p></details><details><summary>Can I connect more than one calendar?</summary><p>Yes. Add up to eight private Google Calendar iCal subscriptions for a merged, read-only agenda and five-minute reminders. Edits depend on when Google publishes them to the feed.</p></details><details><summary>Is Alt+Space Search available to download?</summary><p>Search is in development. The playground demonstrates it with sample data. The current public download is 0.6.3 and does not include Search, the new Search design or the minimize-to-edge refinement.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="get-it"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">MAKE A LITTLE ROOM</span><h2>Your desktop.<br/>With Floatlet.</h2><a class="button primary" href="/download/">Get the Windows preview ↓</a><p>Free. MIT licensed. Yours to explore.</p></div></section></Layout>
